{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"universal-patchy-perch","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context / Problem\n\nThe shared checkout contains an uncommitted `.codex/config.toml` adjustment that allows the project Serena MCP server’s `write_memory` tool. Because the change is not tracked through review, it contributes to the dirty checkout that cannot fast-forward cleanly to current `origin/main`. The setting should be landed independently through the normal Gerrit process without touching the unrelated local `src/rebar/llm/structured_run.py` work.\n\n## Approach\n\n- Add `[mcp_servers.serena.tools.write_memory]` with `approval_mode = \"approve\"` to `.codex/config.toml`.\n- Validate the file as TOML and assert the effective nested value exactly.\n- Run the repository’s config-relevant and canonical static gates, then send the isolated one-file commit through Gerrit.\n\n## Scope / File Impact\n\n- `.codex/config.toml` only.\n- Do not modify, move, stash, or otherwise disturb the unrelated local `src/rebar/llm/structured_run.py` change in the shared checkout.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] [code-verifiable] Parsing `.codex/config.toml` yields `mcp_servers.serena.tools.write_memory.approval_mode == \"approve\"`.\n- [ ] [code-verifiable] The isolated diff changes only `.codex/config.toml` and preserves all existing Serena command, arguments, environment, and tool approval entries.\n- [ ] [code-verifiable] Repository lint and typecheck gates pass from the worktree virtualenv.\n- [ ] [operator-attested] Gerrit reports `LLM-Review +1`, `Verified +1`, and no unresolved comments before Submit.","id":"6faf-f1ca-1ed2-44da","parent_id":"","priority":1,"tags":["codex","serena","configuration"],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Allow Serena write_memory in Codex project config"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785725399626850001,"uuid":"3f53d9ec-f683-44d1-91ee-f2c323588b6b"}